# SABOTAGE: WS-NOTES/ADR-040 §5.9 — THE TRASH READS THE LIVE SET
# `Reads.trash/2` is the trash view's ONLY read seam, and the one line that makes it a trash is
# `for_read(:archived)` — the `OnlyArchived` read `archivable: true` injects. Dropping it leaves an
# ordinary `Doc` read, which is archive-FILTERED: the deleted page is absent and every live page is
# listed instead. The surface looks healthy — a list renders, each row has a Restore — and only the
# "is the deleted page actually here?" assertion separates a trash from a second index.
#
# Aimed at the READ only. `Writes.restore_page/3` (the `:restore` action, the audit row and the
# link re-derivation), the org scope, the plane posture and the route are all untouched.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/notes_trash_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: a deleted page is here, a live page is not
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/notes/reads.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/notes/reads.ex
@@ -194,8 +194,7 @@
   def trash(mount, scope) do
     rows =
       doc_resource(mount)
-      |> Ash.Query.for_read(:archived)
       |> Ash.Query.ensure_selected([:id, :title, :icon, :parent_doc_id, :position, :revision, :archived_at])
       |> Ash.Query.sort(archived_at: :desc)
       |> Ash.Query.limit(@index_limit)
       |> Ash.read!(scope: scope)
